# .trivyignore — Approved Security Exceptions
#
# Each line contains a CVE ID that has been reviewed and explicitly approved
# by the project architect. Trivy will suppress findings listed here so that
# approved exceptions do not block CI.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN   # optional comment explaining the decision
#
# Process:
#   1. A CRITICAL/HIGH CVE appears in CI and blocks the pipeline.
#   2. The responsible agent or developer documents the CVE in
#      docs/security-exceptions.md with justification.
#   3. The architect reviews and approves by merging the exception.
#   4. The CVE ID is added to this file so Trivy ignores it.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never suppress a CVE without a matching entry in
# docs/security-exceptions.md. Periodically review and remove stale entries.

# --- Approved exceptions below this line ---
# (none yet — add CVE IDs here only after architect approval)
